<task id="031" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Widget Decide lane over MCP shims</title>
    <phase>C Widget</phase>
    <gate>after 022 and 030</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include frontend; modifies .ts/.tsx in the shared lib and the widget</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Reuses WorklistLanePanel, buildLaneView and WorklistService over the 030 shim with explicit FR-12 behaviour and Console reference mount</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns shared-lib Worklist component edits and the widget lane files; 010 and 040 touch none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>022, 030</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, typescript, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Render the Decide lane in the widget by reusing WorklistLanePanel (deep import) with buildLaneView and createWorklistService over the MCP fetch shim — header, category cards, rows grouped by matter, Start review across all pages — with billing Work Items shown only as a link out to Invoice Review and the Console's own worklist unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and extending shared component libraries without breaking existing consumers.</role>
  <goal>The widget shows the Decide lane with Console-equal counts, paging through the app-only page tool; billing rows link out with 'Finding' wording and no decide action; any shared-lib change is an optional seam and every existing Console worklist test passes unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-12, FR-05 (Start review walks the whole lane), D-208 ('Finding' only for billing link-outs). Gotchas: WorklistLanePanel is not exported from the Worklist barrel (deep import + buildLaneView; fallback a single-lane prop on WorklistWidget); openInvoiceReview.ts calls Xrm navigateTo and cannot run here — reuse buildInvoiceReviewLaunch(...).pageInput.data and encode once more inside a URL opened with the host's openLink; the live Console mounts the worklist through worklist.registration.ts.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/lane/DecideLane.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/lane/billingLinkOut.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/DecideLane.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/billingLinkOut.test.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/WorklistLanePanel.tsx (ONLY if needed: optional paging seam, e.g. hasMore/onLoadMore)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/WorklistWidget.tsx (ONLY if standalone mount fails: optional single-lane prop; props L76-102)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/worklistView.ts (buildLaneView)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/laneCountFilters.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/openInvoiceReview.ts (buildInvoiceReviewLaunch L33; data rules only)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/worklist.registration.ts:94-114 (how the Console injects fetch)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/__tests__/WorklistInvoiceReview.test.tsx (billing behaviour to mirror)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="022" status="pending">spaarke_show_decisions and the paging tool (incl. consoleBaseUrl)</dependency>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Widget scaffold and shims</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">This task reuses @spaarke/ui-components by deep import of source modules (not the barrel); it creates no per-project copy of a shared component; any shared-lib change is an optional prop or seam that leaves the Console's LegalWorkspace worklist mount (worklist.registration.ts) unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Shared-lib changes are optional props with defaults that reproduce today's behaviour; LegalWorkspace's worklist.registration.ts, Spaarke.AI.Widgets' WorklistWorkspaceWidget and Spaarke.DailyBriefing's worklist section are not edited, and their tests pass unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Billing Work Items (item.invoiceReview present) render only a link to the Invoice Review page sprk_invoicereviewpage built from consoleBaseUrl with data = 'invoiceId=' + bare lower-case guid (+ '&amp;lineId=' + guid only when present), that data string URL-encoded once in the link, opened via the host openLink; the row says 'Finding', offers no decide action, never opens the wizard and is skipped by Start review (EB-D-194, D-208).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The widget uses no openLookup, openRecord or Xrm call, disables the narrative briefing, and keeps lane open/closed state in localStorage wrapped in try/catch so it degrades safely.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every component this task adds or changes uses Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only (no hex, rgb or inline colour), supports host light and dark themes, and is operable by keyboard (NFR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
