    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Console worklist mount" location="src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/worklist.registration.ts">Lines 94-114 show how fetch and openers are injected; mirror with MCP shims.</pattern>
      <pattern name="GUID case" location=".claude/FAILURE-MODES.md">AP-3: GUID case mismatch; the Invoice Review link uses bare lower-case guids (cleanGuid in openInvoiceReview.ts).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Try mounting WorklistLanePanel standalone via deep import with buildLaneView and createWorklistService({ fetch: mcpFetch }); if it cannot mount, add the optional single-lane prop to WorklistWidget instead; record which in notes/decisions.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire paging: first page from spaarke_show_decisions, later pages from the paging tool through the shim; add an optional paging seam to WorklistLanePanel only if needed.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement billingLinkOut.ts from buildInvoiceReviewLaunch(...).pageInput.data and consoleBaseUrl; render billing rows with 'Finding' wording and no decide action; exclude them from Start review.</step>
    <step order="4">Emit an openWizard(signalId) event for non-billing rows (032 consumes it).</step>
    <step order="5">Write the widget tests; run the shared-lib, LegalWorkspace, AI.Widgets and DailyBriefing worklist tests unchanged; run the bundle-size check.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the ui-tests against a local MCP Apps host with seeded data.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any existing Console worklist test would need an edit, STOP and escalate: the Console must be unchanged (FR-12).</trigger>
    <trigger>If consoleBaseUrl is missing from 022's structuredContent, STOP and raise it against 022 rather than hard-coding a URL.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>WorklistWidget.tsx and WorklistLanePanel.tsx in the shared lib render the Decide lane for the Console; openInvoiceReview.ts (buildInvoiceReviewLaunch L33) opens Invoice Review through Xrm navigateTo.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for rendering: the lane reuses WorklistLanePanel, buildLaneView and createWorklistService unchanged; the only new files are the frame adapter DecideLane.tsx and billingLinkOut.ts, needed because openInvoiceReview.ts calls Xrm navigateTo, which does not exist in the Copilot frame.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The widget shows no Work Items (FR-12), and billing rows would either fail (no Xrm) or offer a decision that must stay in Invoice Review (EB-D-194).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Decide lane renders with Console counts">
      <url>http://localhost:{basic-host-port}/?server={local-bff}/mcp/legal-operations</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Seed a user with 70 Decide-lane items across 3 matters, including 2 billing items</step>
        <step>Load the widget through spaarke_show_decisions</step>
        <step>Verify header 'Decide', the count and 'Items that need your decision'</step>
        <step>Verify category cards (All, Invoice decisions, work types, Other) show count, oldest age and done today, and clicking one filters the rows</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for JavaScript errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Counts equal the Console's Decide lane for the same user; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Billing row links out only">
      <steps>
        <step>Find a billing Work Item row</step>
        <step>Verify it reads 'Finding', has no decide action, and its link opens sprk_invoicereviewpage with invoiceId (and lineId when present)</step>
        <step>Click Start review and verify billing rows are skipped</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The wizard never opens for a billing row</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Start review walks all pages">
      <steps>
        <step>Click Start review</step>
        <step>Advance through items and verify the position label ('2 of 70')</step>
        <step>Verify the last item is reached across page boundaries</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every non-billing item is reachable</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Loading, empty and error states">
      <steps>
        <step>Delay the tool response and verify a loading state</step>
        <step>Return zero items and verify the empty state</step>
        <step>Return an isError result and verify the error state with the server message</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each state renders with Fluent components</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host (Cowork or the local MCP Apps host) to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds adapt (no white surface in dark mode) and text adapts (no black text in dark mode)</step>
        <step>Verify icons use currentColor</step>
        <step>Switch back to light theme and verify the widget follows without reload</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours come from Fluent v9 semantic tokens driven by host context (ADR-021); nothing is stored</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund), build and test TypeScript projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/lane/DecideLane.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/lane/billingLinkOut.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/DecideLane.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/billingLinkOut.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The lane renders the header ('Decide', count, 'Items that need your decision'), category cards with count, oldest age and done today (click filters rows), and rows grouped by matter with reason and age.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The lane's counts equal spaarke_show_decisions' per-category counts for the same mocked data.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Start review walks every non-billing item across pages with a 'n of N' label and reaches item 200 in a 200-item mock.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Clicking a non-billing row emits openWizard(signalId).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A billing row renders 'Finding', a link to sprk_invoicereviewpage whose data is invoiceId={lower-case guid} plus &amp;lineId={lower-case guid} only when present, encoded once in the URL; it has no decide action and never opens the wizard.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a billing item with no invoiceId renders no link and no decide action (unit test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Loading, empty and error states render; an isError result shows the server's message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing shared-lib Worklist tests (including WorklistInvoiceReview and laneCountFilters), LegalWorkspace, AI.Widgets and DailyBriefing worklist tests pass with no edits.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No hex or inline colour in the widget source (grep); lane and rows are keyboard-operable; dist/index.html stays under 3 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-12 acceptance 'in Cowork, /spaarke-decisions renders the lane' is verified live in 042. 'Finding' is the user word only for billing link-outs (D-208); generic rows say 'Work Item'.</notes>

